# Documentation upkeep

- After each meaningful development stage, update `README.md` and `docs/development-record.md` before reporting completion.
- Keep working, simulated and unfinished behaviour explicit. Update setup, walkthroughs, screenshots and file links when affected.
- Record significant decisions, AI-assisted adaptations and checks actually performed. Preserve dated history; do not invent results or label old checks as new.
- Recalculate the README prose word count after prose edits, verify affected relative links and run the documentation formatting check.
- Before final submission, reconcile README, report, diagram and storyboards with the implemented version, and add the real repository/README links and submitted commit or release once designated.

- End each user-facing turn about this project with a short completed/remaining checklist, as Hassan requested. Keep it current and distinguish prepared review artefacts from final publication or submission.
